	<interface name="TransformUniformContext" c:type="OmniTransformUniformContext" c:symbol-prefix="transform_uniform_context" glib:type-name="OmniTransformUniformContext" glib:get-type="omni_transform_uniform_context_get_type" glib:type-struct="TransformUniformContextIface">
		<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Provides context information and methods for
[method@Omni.TransformerState.transform_uniform_async].</doc>
		<prerequisite name="GObject.Object"/>
		<method name="blocked_by" c:identifier="omni_transform_uniform_context_blocked_by">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Indicate that the operation was blocked due to lack of input data in the
specified input stream.

Specifically, calling this method signals that the system must first
increase `WT(input_stream_i, scan_start)` (by materializing the
corresponding range of `input_stream_i`) for the transformer to make
progress.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.TransformUniformContext" c:type="OmniTransformUniformContext*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="input_stream_i" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="guint" c:type="guint"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="scan_start" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Time" c:type="OmniTime"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="blocked_by" invoker="blocked_by">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Indicate that the operation was blocked due to lack of input data in the
specified input stream.

Specifically, calling this method signals that the system must first
increase `WT(input_stream_i, scan_start)` (by materializing the
corresponding range of `input_stream_i`) for the transformer to make
progress.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.TransformUniformContext" c:type="OmniTransformUniformContext*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="input_stream_i" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="guint" c:type="guint"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="scan_start" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Time" c:type="OmniTime"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
		<method name="advance" c:identifier="omni_transform_uniform_context_advance">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Advance the output partial watermark (`WT(Sₒ, this.start)`) to
`time_end`.

Call this method adds range `ΔmSTR = [this.start, time_end)` to every
output stream `Sₒ`'s materialized time range `mSTR(Sₒ)`, thereby marking
the output stream range `ΔmSTR` as materialized.
After a call, `this.start`'s value is updated to `time_end`, allowing the
transformer to repeat the same procedure until a batch is returned or
`time.start` reaches `time.end`.

Before calling this method, the caller must call [method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.depend_on] and
[method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.append_batch] as necessary to return the output batches for `ΔmSTR`
and the associated input dependencies.

`time_end` must be greater than `this.start` and less than or equal
to `this.end`.
    </doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.TransformUniformContext" c:type="OmniTransformUniformContext*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="time_end" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Time" c:type="OmniTime"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="advance" invoker="advance">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Advance the output partial watermark (`WT(Sₒ, this.start)`) to
`time_end`.

Call this method adds range `ΔmSTR = [this.start, time_end)` to every
output stream `Sₒ`'s materialized time range `mSTR(Sₒ)`, thereby marking
the output stream range `ΔmSTR` as materialized.
After a call, `this.start`'s value is updated to `time_end`, allowing the
transformer to repeat the same procedure until a batch is returned or
`time.start` reaches `time.end`.

Before calling this method, the caller must call [method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.depend_on] and
[method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.append_batch] as necessary to return the output batches for `ΔmSTR`
and the associated input dependencies.

`time_end` must be greater than `this.start` and less than or equal
to `this.end`.
    </doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.TransformUniformContext" c:type="OmniTransformUniformContext*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="time_end" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Time" c:type="OmniTime"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
		<method name="depend_on" c:identifier="omni_transform_uniform_context_depend_on">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Add an input stream range that the output depends on.

This method creates an input stream dependency `ID = (Sᵢ, [uₛ, uₑ))` for
`ΔmSTR` (the output time range starting at `this.start` and ending at the
`time_end` value provided to the next call to [method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.advance]).

`stream_i` specifies an input stream index.

An input stream dependency represents the following claims:

- Dependency: "`[uₛ, uₑ) ⊆ mSTR(Sᵢ)` was required to materialize
  `ΔmSTR`".
  This allows the system to invoke the transformer again when the input
  changes.

- Obsolescence: "`[-∞, uₛ) ⊆ mSTR(Sᵢ)` will not be necessary for future
  transformation operations with a larger value of `time.start`."
  This allows the system to discard obsolete intermediate results that
  will not be used in the future.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.TransformUniformContext" c:type="OmniTransformUniformContext*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="input_stream_i" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="guint" c:type="guint"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="start" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Time" c:type="OmniTime"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="end" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Time" c:type="OmniTime"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="depend_on" invoker="depend_on">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Add an input stream range that the output depends on.

This method creates an input stream dependency `ID = (Sᵢ, [uₛ, uₑ))` for
`ΔmSTR` (the output time range starting at `this.start` and ending at the
`time_end` value provided to the next call to [method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.advance]).

`stream_i` specifies an input stream index.

An input stream dependency represents the following claims:

- Dependency: "`[uₛ, uₑ) ⊆ mSTR(Sᵢ)` was required to materialize
  `ΔmSTR`".
  This allows the system to invoke the transformer again when the input
  changes.

- Obsolescence: "`[-∞, uₛ) ⊆ mSTR(Sᵢ)` will not be necessary for future
  transformation operations with a larger value of `time.start`."
  This allows the system to discard obsolete intermediate results that
  will not be used in the future.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.TransformUniformContext" c:type="OmniTransformUniformContext*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="input_stream_i" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="guint" c:type="guint"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="start" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Time" c:type="OmniTime"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="end" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Time" c:type="OmniTime"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
		<method name="append_batch" c:identifier="omni_transform_uniform_context_append_batch">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Add an Arrow record batch to push to an output stream.

The record batch covers `ΔmSTR` (the output time range starting at
`this.start` and ending at the `time_end` value provided to the next call
to [method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.advance]).

Before calling [method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.advance]:

- If `ΔmSTR ⊆ fSTR(Sₒ)` for every output stream `Sₒ`, this method must be
  called for every output stream.
  The `i`-th call pushes to the `i`-th output stream.

- If `ΔmSTR ∩ fSTR(Sₒ) = ∅` for every output stream, this method must not
  be called.

- Other cases are not allowed.
  This means that advancements must be split so that every `ΔmSTR` is
  completely inside or outside `fSTR(Sₒ)`.

The schema must be compatible with that of the output stream in terms of
buffer layout. A null value is treated as a batch with zero rows.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.TransformUniformContext" c:type="OmniTransformUniformContext*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="batch" transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1">
					<type name="Omni.ArrowRecordBatch" c:type="OmniArrowRecordBatch*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="append_batch" invoker="append_batch">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Add an Arrow record batch to push to an output stream.

The record batch covers `ΔmSTR` (the output time range starting at
`this.start` and ending at the `time_end` value provided to the next call
to [method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.advance]).

Before calling [method@Omni.TransformUniformContext.advance]:

- If `ΔmSTR ⊆ fSTR(Sₒ)` for every output stream `Sₒ`, this method must be
  called for every output stream.
  The `i`-th call pushes to the `i`-th output stream.

- If `ΔmSTR ∩ fSTR(Sₒ) = ∅` for every output stream, this method must not
  be called.

- Other cases are not allowed.
  This means that advancements must be split so that every `ΔmSTR` is
  completely inside or outside `fSTR(Sₒ)`.

The schema must be compatible with that of the output stream in terms of
buffer layout. A null value is treated as a batch with zero rows.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
