		</virtual-method>
		<method name="execute_query_async" c:identifier="omni_pipeline_snapshot_execute_query_async">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Execute a prepared query and get the result as a single record batch.

# Query Parameters


`param_values` optionally specifies query parameters. If specified, it
must take one of the following two forms:

- `param_values` conforming to `a{s*}` specifies named parameters, i.e.,
  each placeholder is replaced with the parameter value with the matching
  name. This form is not implemented yet.

- `param_values` conforming to `a*` (but not `a{s*}`) specifies
  positional parameters, i.e., each placeholder is replaced wtih the
  parameter value with the matching position within the array.

It is not possible to mix both forms.


Parameter values are converted to an Arrow scalar value according to the
following algorithm:

 1. If the provided variant is a boxed variant (`v`), execute this
    algorithm on the inner variant.

 2. If the provided variant represents a `nothing` value, return a null
    value.

 3. If the provided variant represents a `just` value, execute this
    algorithm on the inner variant.

 4. Convert the provided variant according to the following conversion
    table.

    | Signature  | Arrow datatype |
    | ---------- | -------------- |
    | `b`        | `Boolean`      |
    | `y`        | `UInt8`        |
    | `n`        | `Int16`        |
    | `q`        | `UInt16`       |
    | `i`        | `Int32`        |
    | `u`        | `UInt32`       |
    | `x`        | `Int64`        |
    | `t`        | `UInt64`       |
    | `d`        | `Float64`      |
    | `s`        | `Utf8`         |
    | `ay`       | `Binary`       |

 5. If the provided variant does not match any of the above types, raise
    an unsupported error.

Currently the resulting Arrow datatype must exactly match the expected
one. Type coercion and nested types may be implemented in the future.

It is unspecified whether a `nothing` value of an unsupported type
(e.g., `@mh nothing`) causes an error.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="none">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.PipelineSnapshot" c:type="OmniPipelineSnapshot*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="query" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.PipelineQuery" c:type="OmniPipelineQuery*"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="param_values" transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1">
					<type name="GLib.Variant" c:type="GVariant*"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="cancellable" transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1">
					<type name="Gio.Cancellable" c:type="GCancellable*"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="callback" transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1" closure="4" scope="async">
					<type name="Gio.AsyncReadyCallback" c:type="GAsyncReadyCallback"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="user_data" transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1">
					<type name="gpointer" c:type="void*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<method name="execute_query_finish" c:identifier="omni_pipeline_snapshot_execute_query_finish" throws="1">
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="Omni.ArrowRecordBatch" c:type="OmniArrowRecordBatch*"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.PipelineSnapshot" c:type="OmniPipelineSnapshot*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="_res_" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Gio.AsyncResult" c:type="GAsyncResult*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="execute_query_async" invoker="execute_query_async">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Execute a prepared query and get the result as a single record batch.

# Query Parameters


