		<method name="plan_async" c:identifier="omni_source_snapshot_plan_async">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Create an `Omni.SourcePlan` object to serve given links for each port.

At least one `Omni.PortLinkSet` is given.
`Omni.PortLinkSet.port_index` refers to a port from the
`Omni.SourceSnapshot` object on which this method is called, and
no two `Omni.PortLinkSet` objects refer to the same port.

Each `Omni.PortLinkSet` object contains at least one
parameter set (`GLib.Variant`).

# Link Outputs

This method must assign a link output set for every link in every
provided [iface@Omni.PortLinkSet] object by calling its methods.

A link output set is a variant of type `a{sv}` (variant dictionary).
It may contain handles (type `h`) referencing input streams created by
[method@Omni.SourcePlanContext.add_table_stream]. The handle values can
be retrieved by the [property@Omni.StreamBuilder:handle] property.

The API provides no built-in mechanisms to define or enforce the schema
of link outputs. The recommended way is to define a schema and an
input port attribute to indicate compliance to that schema through
out-of-band means such as documentation.

# Error Reporting

If the input source needs to validate link parameters,
implementing the validation in this method will result in an optimal
user experience.
    </doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="none">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
