		<method name="finish" c:identifier="omni_source_activate_context_finish">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Signal to the system that the input source has completed its job.

The input source must call this method under the following circumstances:

- **Start failure:**
  After a call to [method@Omni.ActiveSource.start], if the operation is
  unsuccessful (or successfully cancelled), the input source must call
  this method to report the error.
  `error` must be non-null in this case.

- **End of data collection:**
  After calling [method@Omni.SourceActivateContext.started], the input
  source must call this method at some point to indicate that data
  collection has stopped.
  Normally, this occurs after [method@Omni.ActiveSource.stop] is called.
  However, it may also be called earlier based on an
  implementation-specific trigger (e.g., when the target is no longer
  running), even inside `start`.
  `error` must be null in this case.

- **Cancelling data collection:**
  After a call to [method@Omni.ActiveSource.cancel], the input source must
  call this method to indicate that data collection has been fully
  cancelled.
  `error` must be null in this case.</doc>
