					<type name="Gio.Cancellable" c:type="GCancellable*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="start" invoker="start">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Start data collection.

This operation can be done only once, whether successful or not, for
each instance of this object.

The input source must attempt to start collection and call one of the
following methods:

- [method@Omni.SourceActivateContext.started] if successful

- [method@Omni.SourceActivateContext.finish] with non-null error
  if unsuccessful.

Calling the above methods synchronously from `start` is allowed.

After calling [method@Omni.SourceActivateContext.started], this method
may immediately and synchronously call
[method@Omni.SourceActivateContext.finish] with null error if there is no
data to produce.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.ActiveSource" c:type="OmniActiveSource*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="cancellable" transfer-ownership="none" nullable="1">
					<type name="Gio.Cancellable" c:type="GCancellable*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
		<method name="stop" c:identifier="omni_active_source_stop">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Stop data collection previously started by calling `start`, and then
deactivate the input source.

The input source must cease data collection as soon as possible and call
[method@Omni.SourceActivateContext.finish].
Calling it synchronously from `stop` is allowed.

Note that [method@Omni.SourceActivateContext.finish] can only be called
exactly once after the end of data collection. If the input source has
already called it due to its own trigger, it must not do it again.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
