	<interface name="Tool" c:type="OmniTool" c:symbol-prefix="tool" glib:type-name="OmniTool" glib:get-type="omni_tool_get_type" glib:type-struct="ToolIface">
		<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">An analysis tool instance.

Classes implementing this interface may expose properties to enable
customization of tool parameters. The following property type is handled
specially:

- A property of type `Omni.LinkArray` is presented to the user as a
  field to specify filtering criteria of input ports, which is then resolved
  to specific input ports when instantiating the tool instance.

  A session configuration stores the filtering criteria instead of the
  resolved `Omni.LinkArray`. As such, this type of property is not
  required to be variant-compatible.

  A property of this type must have an `Omni.LinkPolicy` assigned to
  it.

The remaining property types must be `GLib.Variant` or other
variant-compatible fundamental types.

The properites of type [type@GLib.Variant] are assumed non-nullable. They
must have non-null default values. Wrap them with a maybe type (`m*`) to
make them optional.

# Variant-compatible Types


The following value types are considered variant-compatible:

| `G_TYPE_*`   | C                 | Variant Type |
| ------------ | ----------------- | ------------ |
| `BOOLEAN`    | `gboolean`        | `b`          |
| `BYTES`      | `GBytes *`        | `may`        |
| `DOUBLE`     | `gdouble`         | `d`          |
| `INT`        | `gint`            | `i`          |
| `INT64`      | `gint64`          | `x`          |
| `STRING`     | `char *`          | `ms`         |
| `STRV`       | `char **`         | `as`         |
| `UCHAR`      | `guchar`/`guint8` | `y`          |
| `UINT`       | `guint`           | `u`          |
| `UINT64`     | `guint64`         | `t`          |
| `VARIANT`    | `GVariant *`      | `*`          |</doc>
		<prerequisite name="GObject.Object"/>
		<method name="list_active_port_properties" c:identifier="omni_tool_list_active_port_properties" throws="1">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Enumerate all active port property names.

This method is called during planning to allow tools to conditionally
exclude some port properties from participating in link resolution and
tool instance duplication.
Other properties already have their values set when this method is
called.

The default implementation returns all properties of type
[iface@Omni.LinkArray] and never returns an error.

It is illegal to return properties that the current instance does not
own.

Note that, unlike [method@GObject.ObjectClass.list_properties], the caller
owns the returned elements and is responsible for releasing them when
they are no longer needed. It is designed this way to facilitate the
implementation of memory-safe language bindings.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<array length="0" c:type="gchar**">
					<type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
				</array>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Tool" c:type="OmniTool*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="result_length1" direction="out" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="gint" c:type="gint*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="list_active_port_properties" invoker="list_active_port_properties" throws="1">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Enumerate all active port property names.

This method is called during planning to allow tools to conditionally
exclude some port properties from participating in link resolution and
tool instance duplication.
Other properties already have their values set when this method is
called.

The default implementation returns all properties of type
[iface@Omni.LinkArray] and never returns an error.

It is illegal to return properties that the current instance does not
own.

Note that, unlike [method@GObject.ObjectClass.list_properties], the caller
owns the returned elements and is responsible for releasing them when
they are no longer needed. It is designed this way to facilitate the
implementation of memory-safe language bindings.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<array length="0" c:type="gchar**">
					<type name="utf8" c:type="gchar*"/>
				</array>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Tool" c:type="OmniTool*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="result_length1" direction="out" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="gint" c:type="gint*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
		<method name="modify_links" c:identifier="omni_tool_modify_links" throws="1">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Extend link parameter sets.

This method is called during planning to give tools an opportunity to
override resolved links' parameter sets ([property@Omni.Link:param-set])
before they are passed to input sources.

The default implementation does nothing, and this serves most use cases.
Tool implementations need to override this method only if additional
link parameters are required by the port schema.

The method implementation can assume that all active port properties
(returned by [method@Omni.Tool.list_active_port_properties]) are set to a non-null
value and contain the links that need to be modified.
</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Tool" c:type="OmniTool*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="modify_links" invoker="modify_links" throws="1">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Extend link parameter sets.

This method is called during planning to give tools an opportunity to
override resolved links' parameter sets ([property@Omni.Link:param-set])
before they are passed to input sources.

The default implementation does nothing, and this serves most use cases.
Tool implementations need to override this method only if additional
link parameters are required by the port schema.

The method implementation can assume that all active port properties
(returned by [method@Omni.Tool.list_active_port_properties]) are set to a non-null
value and contain the links that need to be modified.
</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.Tool" c:type="OmniTool*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
		<method name="add_to_pipeline" c:identifier="omni_tool_add_to_pipeline" throws="1">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Add components to a pipeline, using information from the object's
properties and the link outputs provided by [property@Omni.Link:output-set].</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
