	<interface name="ProjectOpBuilder" c:type="OmniProjectOpBuilder" c:symbol-prefix="project_op_builder" glib:type-name="OmniProjectOpBuilder" glib:get-type="omni_project_op_builder_get_type" glib:type-struct="ProjectOpBuilderIface">
		<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Defines the details of a projection operator in [iface@Omni.PipelineBuilder].

# Point-wise Operation


This operator requires that the primary partitioning key (PPK) of every
output stream be an exact copy of an input PPK.
To enforce this, the operator requires that the output PPK value is defined
via [method@ProjectOpBuilder.append_field_copy], and its value must originate
from an input PPK field in all cases.


Furthermore, the intermediate result from every node must have at least one
field eligible as an output PPK.

&gt; Example: Suppose the union of two input streams `{time, foo}` and
&gt; `{bar, time}` (`time` is the PPK in both) is used as the projection input.
&gt; This yields two output fields, but neither is suitable as an output PPK.

# Input Graph

Each instance of [iface@Omni.ProjectOpBuilder] owns an input node graph,
where each node represents an input stream or a set of input streams
combined in a particular way.
The following methods create input nodes:

- [method@ProjectOpBuilder.append_input_stream]
- [method@ProjectOpBuilder.filter_input_with_sql]
- [method@ProjectOpBuilder.union_inputs]
- [method@ProjectOpBuilder.join_inputs]

Each node is represented by an opaque handle value that is only valid inside
the [iface@Omni.ProjectOpBuilder] in which the node was created.

&gt; Note: A node handle can take any value.
&gt; There is no value reserved to represent an invalid handle.

Each node except for an input stream can only be used by a single node.


One node is designated as the input to the final projection stage by calling
[method@ProjectOpBuilder.set_source_input].

# Projection

The projection stage derives each output field's value using provided
expressions.
The following methods define output fields:

- [method@ProjectOpBuilder.append_field_copy_all]
- [method@ProjectOpBuilder.append_field_copy]
- [method@ProjectOpBuilder.append_field_with_sql]


If there is a type mismatch in an output field, the projection expression is
implicitly converted to the output field type. Planning will fail if the
conversion is not supported.

# Multi-Output

This operator can be configured with multiple output streams.
It operates as if an independent instance of the operator is created for each
output stream.
However, intermediate computation results are reused among different
instances to reduce duplicated work, so a single multi-output operator is
more efficient than using multiple single-output operators to achieve the
same effect.

&gt; Currently, this is implemented by expanding a multi-output projection
&gt; operator into single-output ones, so there is no performance benefit.
&gt; Native multi-output support is planned in the future.
&gt; 

All instances behave identically by default.
Operator components can be disabled for specific instances using the
following properties:

- [property@Omni.ProjectFieldBuilder:output_stream]
- [property@Omni.ProjectFilterBuilder:output_stream]

# SQL Column References


Field references are resolved against the operand of a filter node, or
against the source node in projection expressions.
`"table[i]"."field"` names a column whose value is fed by input stream `i`.
The `"table[i]"` qualifier can be omitted when the field name is unambiguous.


Identifiers in a column reference must be double-quoted.

# Supported SQL Subset

The following features can be used in SQL expressions in field and filter
definitions:

- Deterministic scalar functions and operators
- Column references
- Literals

The following are not supported:

- Aggregation functions
- Window functions
- Subqueries
- Wildcards
- `UNNEST`

# Return Type Conventions

For convenience in simple cases, these methods return builder objects through
optional out parameters.
    </doc>
		<prerequisite name="GObject.Object"/>
		<method name="append_output_stream" c:identifier="omni_project_op_builder_append_output_stream">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Append a stream to the output stream list.

Each output stream is assigned an index in the calling order, starting
from zero.
