	<interface name="TrackBuilder" c:type="OmniTrackBuilder" c:symbol-prefix="track_builder" glib:type-name="OmniTrackBuilder" glib:get-type="omni_track_builder_get_type" glib:type-struct="TrackBuilderIface">
		<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Defines the details of a timeline track in `Omni.PipelineBuilder`.</doc>
		<prerequisite name="GObject.Object"/>
		<method name="append_group_field_with_sql" c:identifier="omni_track_builder_append_group_field_with_sql">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Append a subtrack grouping field.

`sql` must be an SQL expression in the following form:

- `"field_name"`: Use the value of the input field named `field_name`
  for grouping.


A visualizer in this track is considered subtrack-compatible if the
visualizer type supports subtracks and every input stream subject to
subtrack grouping contains all columns referenced by `sql`.
`sql` must evaluate to the same type for every subtrack-compatible
visualizer in this track.

If [property@Omni.TrackBuilder:group-values] is set, `sql` must evaluate to
the same type as the corresponding column in that record batch.
Calling this method `N` times requires `group_values` to contain `N`
columns.
If this method is never called, grouping field specifications are
inferred from `group_values` without additional constraints.

If [property@Omni.TrackBuilder:group-values] is `null`, calling this method
enables dynamic subtracks. The session creates a subtrack for each
grouping key discovered in the input streams of subtrack-compatible
visualizers.
    </doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="Omni.GroupFieldBuilder" c:type="OmniGroupFieldBuilder*"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.TrackBuilder" c:type="OmniTrackBuilder*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="sql" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="append_group_field_with_sql" invoker="append_group_field_with_sql">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Append a subtrack grouping field.

`sql` must be an SQL expression in the following form:

- `"field_name"`: Use the value of the input field named `field_name`
  for grouping.


A visualizer in this track is considered subtrack-compatible if the
visualizer type supports subtracks and every input stream subject to
subtrack grouping contains all columns referenced by `sql`.
`sql` must evaluate to the same type for every subtrack-compatible
visualizer in this track.

If [property@Omni.TrackBuilder:group-values] is set, `sql` must evaluate to
the same type as the corresponding column in that record batch.
Calling this method `N` times requires `group_values` to contain `N`
columns.
If this method is never called, grouping field specifications are
inferred from `group_values` without additional constraints.

If [property@Omni.TrackBuilder:group-values] is `null`, calling this method
enables dynamic subtracks. The session creates a subtrack for each
grouping key discovered in the input streams of subtrack-compatible
visualizers.
    </doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
