		<method name="append_span_layer" c:identifier="omni_rich_summary_builder_append_span_layer">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Append a span layer after the existing layers in this summary view.
Layers are drawn in this order, so later layers appear in front of
earlier layers.

# Schema

```text
table $start_stream&lt;Id&gt; {
    [primary_partitioning_key]
    $time_field_name: Int64,
    $id_field_name: Id,
    [optional] $label_field_name: String,
    [optional] $color_field_name: Int32,
    [for each subtrack grouping field]
    $subtrack_group_field_name: T,
}

table $end_stream&lt;Id&gt; {
    [primary_partitioning_key]
    $time_field_name: Int64,
    $id_field_name: Id,
    [if($cross_subtrack)]
    [for each subtrack grouping field]
    $subtrack_group_field_name: T,
}
```

Field `id_field_name` provides span IDs, which are used to associate
start and end events. All IDs must be unique within the streams.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
