	<interface name="PlotSeriesBuilder" c:type="OmniPlotSeriesBuilder" c:symbol-prefix="plot_series_builder" glib:type-name="OmniPlotSeriesBuilder" glib:get-type="omni_plot_series_builder_get_type" glib:type-struct="PlotSeriesBuilderIface">
		<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Defines a data series of a plot layer in a plot summary view.

A data series is a visual representation of a single field from a source stream.</doc>
		<prerequisite name="GObject.Object"/>
		<method name="append_value_color_stop" c:identifier="omni_plot_series_builder_append_value_color_stop">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Append a gradient color stop for value-dependent coloring.

Adding at least one stop enables value-dependent coloring, overriding the
default color of the series.

The color stops must be added in the increasing order of values.
The colors for values falling in-between are determined by interpolating
the adjacent color stops.
Add two stops with an identical value to create discontinuity.

# Special colors

The following special color values are supported:

* [const@Omni.COLOR_DEFAULT]
* [const@Omni.COLOR_WARNING]
* [const@Omni.COLOR_DANGER]
    </doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.PlotSeriesBuilder" c:type="OmniPlotSeriesBuilder*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="value" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="gdouble" c:type="gdouble"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="color" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="guint32" c:type="guint32"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="append_value_color_stop" invoker="append_value_color_stop">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Append a gradient color stop for value-dependent coloring.

Adding at least one stop enables value-dependent coloring, overriding the
default color of the series.

The color stops must be added in the increasing order of values.
The colors for values falling in-between are determined by interpolating
the adjacent color stops.
Add two stops with an identical value to create discontinuity.

# Special colors

The following special color values are supported:

* [const@Omni.COLOR_DEFAULT]
* [const@Omni.COLOR_WARNING]
* [const@Omni.COLOR_DANGER]
    </doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="none" c:type="void"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.PlotSeriesBuilder" c:type="OmniPlotSeriesBuilder*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="value" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="gdouble" c:type="gdouble"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="color" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="guint32" c:type="guint32"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
	</interface>
	<record name="PlotSeriesBuilderIface" c:type="OmniPlotSeriesBuilderIface" glib:is-gtype-struct-for="PlotSeriesBuilder">
		<field name="parent_iface" readable="0" private="1">
			<type name="GObject.TypeInterface" c:type="GTypeInterface"/>
		</field>
		<field name="append_value_color_stop">
