	<interface name="AggregationDetailBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationDetailBuilder" c:symbol-prefix="aggregation_detail_builder" glib:type-name="OmniAggregationDetailBuilder" glib:get-type="omni_aggregation_detail_builder_get_type" glib:type-struct="AggregationDetailBuilderIface">
		<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Defines an aggregation detail view.</doc>
		<prerequisite name="Omni.DetailBuilder"/>
		<method name="append_stream" c:identifier="omni_aggregation_detail_builder_append_stream">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Add a source stream.

A group is outputted if and only if there exists at least one source
stream containing a row with the matching grouping field values.

&gt; Current Limitation: Only the first stream generates groups.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="Omni.AggregationStreamBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationStreamBuilder*"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.AggregationDetailBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationDetailBuilder*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="stream_handle" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="gint32" c:type="gint32"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="time_field_name" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="append_stream" invoker="append_stream">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Add a source stream.

A group is outputted if and only if there exists at least one source
stream containing a row with the matching grouping field values.

&gt; Current Limitation: Only the first stream generates groups.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="Omni.AggregationStreamBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationStreamBuilder*"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.AggregationDetailBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationDetailBuilder*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="stream_handle" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="gint32" c:type="gint32"/>
				</parameter>
				<parameter name="time_field_name" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
		<method name="append_column_with_sql" c:identifier="omni_aggregation_detail_builder_append_column_with_sql">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Append a new column with a custom SQL expression.

The SQL expression can refer to grouping fields directly, or to other
fields inside aggregate functions. For example, a SQL expression
`SUM("table[0]"."x")` displays the sum of the first source stream's field
named `x` for each group.
The table name can be omitted if there is exactly one source stream.

&gt; Current Limitation: The SQL expression can only refer to the first

&gt; Current Limitation: The table name can be omitted even if there are
&gt; multiple source streams.
&gt; This behavior is a bug and must not be relied upon.

Each aggregation function invocation must reference fields from
exactly one source stream.
The asterisk syntax (e.g., `COUNT(*)`) is not allowed.

Window functions are not supported.

The following placeholders can be used in the SQL expression:

- `$time_start[0]`/`$time_end[0]`: Replaced with the time filtering
  range.
  This range is bounded by the stream time range (fSTR).
  The stream index must be an integer literal.

- `$time_start`/`$time_end`: Shorthand for
  `$time_start[0]`/`$time_end[0]` available if there is exactly one input
  stream.

&gt; Note: Using placeholders can degrade performance.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="Omni.AggregationColumnBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationColumnBuilder*"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.AggregationDetailBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationDetailBuilder*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="expr" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</method>
		<virtual-method name="append_column_with_sql" invoker="append_column_with_sql">
			<doc xml:whitespace="preserve" filename="" line="0">Append a new column with a custom SQL expression.

The SQL expression can refer to grouping fields directly, or to other
fields inside aggregate functions. For example, a SQL expression
`SUM("table[0]"."x")` displays the sum of the first source stream's field
named `x` for each group.
The table name can be omitted if there is exactly one source stream.

&gt; Current Limitation: The SQL expression can only refer to the first

&gt; Current Limitation: The table name can be omitted even if there are
&gt; multiple source streams.
&gt; This behavior is a bug and must not be relied upon.

Each aggregation function invocation must reference fields from
exactly one source stream.
The asterisk syntax (e.g., `COUNT(*)`) is not allowed.

Window functions are not supported.

The following placeholders can be used in the SQL expression:

- `$time_start[0]`/`$time_end[0]`: Replaced with the time filtering
  range.
  This range is bounded by the stream time range (fSTR).
  The stream index must be an integer literal.

- `$time_start`/`$time_end`: Shorthand for
  `$time_start[0]`/`$time_end[0]` available if there is exactly one input
  stream.

&gt; Note: Using placeholders can degrade performance.</doc>
			<return-value transfer-ownership="full">
				<type name="Omni.AggregationColumnBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationColumnBuilder*"/>
			</return-value>
			<parameters>
				<instance-parameter name="self" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="Omni.AggregationDetailBuilder" c:type="OmniAggregationDetailBuilder*"/>
				</instance-parameter>
				<parameter name="expr" transfer-ownership="none">
					<type name="utf8" c:type="const gchar*"/>
				</parameter>
			</parameters>
		</virtual-method>
		<method name="append_group_column" c:identifier="omni_aggregation_detail_builder_append_group_column">
